$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 11/Practice
::HC-W11-P01::A campaign objective is distribute 50,000 leaflets about cervical screening. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=activity stated as objective#Correct. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~strategy-service inconsistency#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~product-first planning#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~comprehension bottleneck#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
}

::HC-W11-P02::A campaign objective is distribute 50,000 leaflets about cervical screening. What is the strongest next response? {
=Rewrite the objective as a measurable audience change such as correct knowledge, confidence or screening intention.#Correct. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~Coordinate commodity and service readiness before intensifying demand generation.#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~Define the problem, audience, behavioural determinant and objective before selecting products or channels.#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
~Revise the message or format and pre-test again rather than merely buying more exposure.#Not the best answer. Distribution is an output, not the communication outcome.
}

::HC-W11-P03::A malaria campaign increases demand for testing during a period of frequent stock-outs. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=strategy-service inconsistency#Correct. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~product-first planning#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~comprehension bottleneck#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~distal outcome as sole objective#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
}

::HC-W11-P04::A malaria campaign increases demand for testing during a period of frequent stock-outs. What is the strongest next response? {
=Coordinate commodity and service readiness before intensifying demand generation.#Correct. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~Define the problem, audience, behavioural determinant and objective before selecting products or channels.#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~Revise the message or format and pre-test again rather than merely buying more exposure.#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
~Add intermediate communication outcomes that are plausibly influenced within the campaign period.#Not the best answer. Communication can damage trust when the promised service is unavailable.
}

::HC-W11-P05::A team designs television advertisements before deciding which audience behaviour it needs to change. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=product-first planning#Correct. Strategy should precede creative production.
~comprehension bottleneck#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
~distal outcome as sole objective#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
~implementation governance gap#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
}

::HC-W11-P06::A team designs television advertisements before deciding which audience behaviour it needs to change. What is the strongest next response? {
=Define the problem, audience, behavioural determinant and objective before selecting products or channels.#Correct. Strategy should precede creative production.
~Revise the message or format and pre-test again rather than merely buying more exposure.#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
~Add intermediate communication outcomes that are plausibly influenced within the campaign period.#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
~Create an implementation matrix with responsibilities, timelines, dependencies and escalation routes.#Not the best answer. Strategy should precede creative production.
}

::HC-W11-P07::Reach is high but correct understanding remains low halfway through a campaign. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=comprehension bottleneck#Correct. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~distal outcome as sole objective#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~implementation governance gap#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~confounded before-after evaluation#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
}

::HC-W11-P08::Reach is high but correct understanding remains low halfway through a campaign. What is the strongest next response? {
=Revise the message or format and pre-test again rather than merely buying more exposure.#Correct. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~Add intermediate communication outcomes that are plausibly influenced within the campaign period.#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~Create an implementation matrix with responsibilities, timelines, dependencies and escalation routes.#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
~Use comparison data or stronger quasi-experimental design and document concurrent changes.#Not the best answer. Monitoring should trigger adaptation at the point of failure.
}
$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 11/Mastery
::HC-W11-M01::A campaign states reduce maternal mortality by 20 percent in three months as its only communication objective. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=distal outcome as sole objective#Correct. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~implementation governance gap#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~confounded before-after evaluation#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~output-heavy monitoring#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
}

::HC-W11-M02::A campaign states reduce maternal mortality by 20 percent in three months as its only communication objective. What is the strongest next response? {
=Add intermediate communication outcomes that are plausibly influenced within the campaign period.#Correct. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~Create an implementation matrix with responsibilities, timelines, dependencies and escalation routes.#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~Use comparison data or stronger quasi-experimental design and document concurrent changes.#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
~Add indicators for exposure, comprehension, trust, intention and behaviour aligned with objectives.#Not the best answer. Mortality is important but too distal to diagnose communication performance alone.
}

::HC-W11-M03::A campaign has clear objectives but no named staff responsible for approvals, media booking or community mobilisation. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=implementation governance gap#Correct. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~confounded before-after evaluation#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~output-heavy monitoring#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~over-broad strategy#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
}

::HC-W11-M04::A campaign has clear objectives but no named staff responsible for approvals, media booking or community mobilisation. What is the strongest next response? {
=Create an implementation matrix with responsibilities, timelines, dependencies and escalation routes.#Correct. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~Use comparison data or stronger quasi-experimental design and document concurrent changes.#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~Add indicators for exposure, comprehension, trust, intention and behaviour aligned with objectives.#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
~Prioritise behaviours and audiences or develop distinct strategic pathways for different decisions.#Not the best answer. A sound strategy can fail through unclear execution.
}

::HC-W11-M05::The evaluation compares service uptake before and after the campaign, while clinic hours and fees also changed. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=confounded before-after evaluation#Correct. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~output-heavy monitoring#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~over-broad strategy#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~capacity dependency failure#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
}

::HC-W11-M06::The evaluation compares service uptake before and after the campaign, while clinic hours and fees also changed. What is the strongest next response? {
=Use comparison data or stronger quasi-experimental design and document concurrent changes.#Correct. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~Add indicators for exposure, comprehension, trust, intention and behaviour aligned with objectives.#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~Prioritise behaviours and audiences or develop distinct strategic pathways for different decisions.#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
~Build service capacity and contingency thresholds into the campaign implementation plan.#Not the best answer. Concurrent interventions weaken attribution to communication.
}

::HC-W11-M07::The dashboard shows posters printed, radio spots aired and social impressions but no audience outcomes. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=output-heavy monitoring#Correct. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~over-broad strategy#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~capacity dependency failure#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~monitoring without adaptive authority#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
}

::HC-W11-M08::The dashboard shows posters printed, radio spots aired and social impressions but no audience outcomes. What is the strongest next response? {
=Add indicators for exposure, comprehension, trust, intention and behaviour aligned with objectives.#Correct. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~Prioritise behaviours and audiences or develop distinct strategic pathways for different decisions.#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~Build service capacity and contingency thresholds into the campaign implementation plan.#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
~Define in advance which indicators can trigger revision and who can authorise changes.#Not the best answer. Outputs cannot show whether the communication pathway worked.
}

::HC-W11-M09::A campaign tries to change three unrelated behaviours for five audiences with one generic slogan. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=over-broad strategy#Correct. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~capacity dependency failure#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~monitoring without adaptive authority#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~messenger dependency risk#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
}

::HC-W11-M10::A campaign tries to change three unrelated behaviours for five audiences with one generic slogan. What is the strongest next response? {
=Prioritise behaviours and audiences or develop distinct strategic pathways for different decisions.#Correct. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~Build service capacity and contingency thresholds into the campaign implementation plan.#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~Define in advance which indicators can trigger revision and who can authorise changes.#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
~Use a diversified messenger strategy and contingency plan rather than relying on one personality.#Not the best answer. A single message is unlikely to address heterogeneous determinants.
}

::HC-W11-M11::A programme reaches its intended audience but the recommended service cannot accommodate increased demand. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=capacity dependency failure#Correct. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~monitoring without adaptive authority#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~messenger dependency risk#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~ecological confounding#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
}

::HC-W11-M12::A programme reaches its intended audience but the recommended service cannot accommodate increased demand. What is the strongest next response? {
=Build service capacity and contingency thresholds into the campaign implementation plan.#Correct. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~Define in advance which indicators can trigger revision and who can authorise changes.#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~Use a diversified messenger strategy and contingency plan rather than relying on one personality.#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
~Adjust or stratify for service readiness and use appropriate design before attributing the gradient to exposure.#Not the best answer. Communication success can create operational failure if capacity is ignored.
}

::HC-W11-M13::Campaign managers refuse to change creative materials because senior leaders already approved them. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=monitoring without adaptive authority#Correct. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~messenger dependency risk#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~ecological confounding#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~outcome switching#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
}

::HC-W11-M14::Campaign managers refuse to change creative materials because senior leaders already approved them. What is the strongest next response? {
=Define in advance which indicators can trigger revision and who can authorise changes.#Correct. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~Use a diversified messenger strategy and contingency plan rather than relying on one personality.#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~Adjust or stratify for service readiness and use appropriate design before attributing the gradient to exposure.#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
~Pre-specify primary indicators and document exploratory analyses separately.#Not the best answer. Monitoring has little value if no decision can follow.
}

::HC-W11-M15::A campaign uses a famous spokesperson whose reputation later becomes controversial. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=messenger dependency risk#Correct. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~ecological confounding#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~outcome switching#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~statistical significance without practical significance#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
}

::HC-W11-M16::A campaign uses a famous spokesperson whose reputation later becomes controversial. What is the strongest next response? {
=Use a diversified messenger strategy and contingency plan rather than relying on one personality.#Correct. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~Adjust or stratify for service readiness and use appropriate design before attributing the gradient to exposure.#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~Pre-specify primary indicators and document exploratory analyses separately.#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
~Interpret effect size, baseline, cost and public-health importance alongside uncertainty.#Not the best answer. Reputational risk can transfer to the campaign.
}
$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Health Communication/Week 11/Institutional
::HC-W11-I01::Service uptake rises most in districts with the highest campaign exposure, and the team claims causality without considering that those districts also had better clinics. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=ecological confounding#Correct. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~outcome switching#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~statistical significance without practical significance#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~activity stated as objective#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
}

::HC-W11-I02::Service uptake rises most in districts with the highest campaign exposure, and the team claims causality without considering that those districts also had better clinics. What is the strongest next response? {
=Adjust or stratify for service readiness and use appropriate design before attributing the gradient to exposure.#Correct. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~Pre-specify primary indicators and document exploratory analyses separately.#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~Interpret effect size, baseline, cost and public-health importance alongside uncertainty.#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
~Rewrite the objective as a measurable audience change such as correct knowledge, confidence or screening intention.#Not the best answer. Exposure and service quality may be correlated.
}

::HC-W11-I03::A campaign evaluator selects indicators after seeing which metrics improved. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=outcome switching#Correct. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~statistical significance without practical significance#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~activity stated as objective#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~strategy-service inconsistency#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
}

::HC-W11-I04::A campaign evaluator selects indicators after seeing which metrics improved. What is the strongest next response? {
=Pre-specify primary indicators and document exploratory analyses separately.#Correct. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~Interpret effect size, baseline, cost and public-health importance alongside uncertainty.#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~Rewrite the objective as a measurable audience change such as correct knowledge, confidence or screening intention.#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
~Coordinate commodity and service readiness before intensifying demand generation.#Not the best answer. Choosing outcomes after results are known inflates positive conclusions.
}

::HC-W11-I05::A programme reports a statistically significant 2 percentage-point change with a huge sample and calls it transformative. Which diagnosis or concept best identifies the main communication issue? {
=statistical significance without practical significance#Correct. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~activity stated as objective#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~strategy-service inconsistency#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~product-first planning#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
}

::HC-W11-I06::A programme reports a statistically significant 2 percentage-point change with a huge sample and calls it transformative. What is the strongest next response? {
=Interpret effect size, baseline, cost and public-health importance alongside uncertainty.#Correct. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~Rewrite the objective as a measurable audience change such as correct knowledge, confidence or screening intention.#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~Coordinate commodity and service readiness before intensifying demand generation.#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
~Define the problem, audience, behavioural determinant and objective before selecting products or channels.#Not the best answer. Large samples can make trivial changes statistically significant.
}

